an excellent opportunity to examine aspects of Early Mycenaean funerary ritual, 
including the engendering of grave goods-topics that are more difficult or 
impossible to address in the case of the much more common Mycenaean chamber and 
tholos tombs built for the interment of multiple individuals over long periods 
of time. The discovery of so many gold rings in incontrovertible association 
