into four zones or “scenes”:  
    - Human figures (including a prominent seated or standing figure, often 
interpreted as a deity or ruler) engaged in ritual acts.  
    - Real animals (e.g., bovines) and possibly mythical creatures in procession
or in association with the figures.  
    - Trees, altars, and other cultic structures.  
    - Boats or riverine elements, plus astral or otherworldly motifs suggesting 
passage to the afterlife.  
